title: AfterPuzzle
// Corresponds to scene 3 in the narrative script
// This scene is from Jovan's POV
// Jovan and his cousin, Sasha, are in this scene
// Sasha is character 1, Jovan is character 2
// NOTE: Sasha is set as character one so his sprite lines up with the chair
---
<<twoChar>>
<<hideChar 1>>
{$cousinName} comes back into the room, puts his plate into the sink and sees {$lover1Name} sitting at the kitchen table.
<<showChar 1>>
<<changeSprite 1 0>>
<<lighten 1>>
{$cousinName}: You know, I know stupid when I see it.
<<darken 1>>

<<lighten 2>>   // Change Jovan's Expresion: Desperate?
{$lover1Name} jumps in his seat, attempting to re-scramble the letter. 
    -> I'm just trying to figure something out.
        {$lover1Name}: I'm just trying to figure something out, {$cousinName}. I told you, it's nothing.
    -> It's not stupid, okay?
        {$lover1Name}: It's not stupid, okay? It's nothing.
    -> Nothing for you to worry about.
        {$lover1Name}: Nothing for you to worry about.
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>   // Change Damir's Expression: Suspicious
{$cousinName}: Nothing? You in the park with a girl is nothing?
<<darken 1>>

<<lighten 2>> // Change Jovan's Expression?
{$lover1Name} freezes. He looks up, meeting {$cousinName}'s eyes.
<<darken 2>>

They stare at each other in silence.

<<lighten 2>>   // Change Jovan's Expression for sure
{$lover1Name} sighs as he realizes there is no point in keeping this secret from {$cousinName}.
{$lover1Name}: Fine. This… girl. She's good, I swear, but she wants me to come meet her. 
{$lover1Name} pauses again, attempting to parse out how much to tell {$cousinName}.
{$lover1Name}: She described a place... a blue house around the corner from an old church made of bricks. 
{$lover1Name}: She said the side of the house would be covered in windows. 
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>   // Change Damir's Expression: Afraid
{$cousinName}'s posture stiffens. His face pales, his expression shifting something akin to fear.
<<darken 1>>

<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: What? What's that look for?
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>
{$cousinName}: It's on the Eskani side of the city.
<<darken 1>>

<<lighten 2>>   // Change Jovan's Expression?
    -> How do you know that?
        {$lover1Name}: How do you know that? You never go over there. No one goes over there.
    -> Are you hiding something?
        {$lover1Name}: And how do you know that? Are you hiding something, {$cousinName}?
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>
{$cousinName} avoids his gaze, staring at a fixed point past his shoulder.
{$cousinName}: This part of town, I was there a long time ago.
<<darken 1>>

<<lighten 2>> // Change Jovan's Expression: Desperate
{$lover1Name} stands and grabs {$cousinName}'s arm, a desperate look on his face.
{$lover1Name}: Then you have to show me. 
{$lover1Name}: I can't find it on this map, and I can't wander around over there looking lost. 
{$lover1Name}: Please, {$cousinName}.
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>   // Change Damir's Expression: Determined
{$cousinName}'s jaw tightens. He looks at the door, then back at {$lover1Name}'s face. 
With a sharp exhale, he moves past {$lover1Name} to the door. 
{$cousinName}: Fine, but let me be clear, {$lover1Name}.
{$cousinName} turns away from the door to look back at {$lover1Name}, a hard look in his eyes. 
{$cousinName}: You're on your own once we're out of the neighborhood.
<<darken 1>>

// After this scene, the characters change
<<nextOrder>>
<<zeroChar>>
===